Z||000000||Bob||10-23-2001||05:00 PM||||Was checking out the GP message board today and it looks like the 3800 SC GP's have been making some improvements. How does 12.755@107.57 in a GP sound?(Heavier and Auto), you can check that at <A HREF="http://www.clubgp.com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6376190&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=OMG%2C++Mike+Dye%27s+NEW+PB%21%21&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General" TARGET=_blank>http://www.clubgp.com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6376190&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=OMG%2C++Mike+Dye%27s+NEW+PB%21%21&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General</A>  . Another one is 12.71@107.74, details at <A HREF="http://www.clubgp.com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6376269&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=MD+sets+a+record+and+ZZP+retorts+w%2F++12%2E71%40107%2E74&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General" TARGET=_blank>http://www.clubgp.com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6376269&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=MD+sets+a+record+and+ZZP+retorts+w%2F++12%2E71%40107%2E74&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General</A>  . Imagine those kind of mods on a L67 Fiero...wow...very possible, very fast.<BR><P>------------------<BR>1997 Pontiac Grand Prix GTP -lotsa mods, so little room...||||reg||11
