Z||000012||Formula88||10-24-2001||10:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>Nah not 300 rwhp just 250 maybe. I'm trying one of Archie's  Centerforces. Hope it's better than the McLeod.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Allright!  Can't wait to hear how that Centerforce holds up to the 3800SC.  If it'll hold 4th gear for you, I'm sold.  Especially when you're finished with your mods.  Didn't you already have a smaller pully on your SC?  I thought you'd be pretty close to 250RWHP already.  A pully should get the engine up to about 280HP at the flywheel (in a GTP).  <P>Just been checking ACE's website, too.  It's looking like either a SBC or 3800SC for me...Now all I gotta do is make up my mind and crap the money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
