Z||000022||pontiacs4me||10-25-2001||04:09 PM||||Dont tell anyone, that is supposed to be a secret.  Ill say this once and once only right here on this thread.  Well first off Travis 1fst2m6 is in the high 12's right now, and he is the fastest v6 car on the forum.  by spring my car will, and thats will, not maybe it will be in the mid to low 11's.  No typo, 11's.  The goal is to be able to pull the front tires on launch.   mid 11's, possibly low.  a friend of mine has a program that with the setup i am going with predicted 11.11 in the 1/4.  dont tell anyone.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Soon to be: L67 powered 87 coupe.<p>[This message has been edited by pontiacs4me (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Wannabe||10-25-2001||06:22 PM||||Someone I met with a 3.8 SC Fiero claimed to have run 11's with NOS. His was the first Fiero I've heard of breaking 12s, although, without a time slip, there's now way of knowing if he was being truthful. It is surprising though, the it's so uncommon to hear of Fieros running in the 12's or below, considering the power that is available with an SBC or 3.8SC swap. You would think that 350hp should be plenty to get a 2800lb car into the 12's.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Slammed Fiero||10-25-2001||06:36 PM||||Up here in Canada there is a guy named Bob Cumpson. I don't know him personally , but I have seen and lusted over his car many times. he runs a built (supposedly) 3.8SC with NOS. I believe the one time he had it to the strip he had problems with it though.<P>Judging by the modificatons on Bob's car I would say Low 12's with Slicks and the NOS.<P>JM ||||reg||1
