Z||000029||grinthock||10-26-2001||12:27 PM||||Somebody has pics of Hot Rod Bob's car.<P>It's a 3.8 Series II super, power pully, balanced, blueprinted, NOS, tubular suspension, 17"'s, the car is TOTALLY done, leather interior, BEAUTIFUL audio system, all digital gauges, polished dash plates, <P>I could go on and on.<P>The car didn't run so well the time I saw it run, he has a tranny issue or something, which was fixed.  He hasn't run at the track much so the poor times could be driver related, but that will fix itself in time.<P>He recently spun a bearing coming back from the michigan show, but the car apparantly is back to life.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||newfie||10-26-2001||01:17 PM||||There is no pride in beating a Jeep 4.0L.  It's a inline-6 that's made for tourqe not speed.  I've owned a couple and they have no trouble twisting the D-shaft off when in 4-lo.  The engine puts out 190 bhp and 200+ tourqe.  It's an awesome engine for what its made for, very rarely rev over 3000.  Low end tourqe.  I wouldn't even consider racing anything in my Jeep let alone a fiero! Unless there was a foot of snow on the road.  Anyway had to pick up for Jeep lovers everywhere.  Just my 2 cents(Owner '95 Jeep YJ, 4.0L, lifted and all that other Jeep stuff)I do plan on buying a 88GT and swapping a 3800 series II SC in the very near future though. I was wondering what the weight differences are in the SBC V8 and 3800 though, anyone know where i can find this info.  If the weight wasn't a big difference I'd probably go V8.||||reg||1
